THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL
====================

1. GEHistoricalImagery -- GPL-3.0-or-later
------------------------------------------
   https://github.com/Mbucari/GEHistoricalImagery
   Copyright (C) Mbucari and contributors

   old-imagery is a Python port of the protocol layer of GEHistoricalImagery, a .NET
   CLI by Mbucari. The Keyhole quadtree addressing, packet decryption, dbRoot
   handling and Esri Wayback logic in src/old_imagery/ are ports of that project's
   LibGoogleEarth and LibEsri assemblies and are derivative works of it.

   Because GEHistoricalImagery is licensed under the GNU General Public License
   version 3, old-imagery as a whole is distributed under the same terms.

   The following files are copied verbatim from that project and carry its
   copyright:

     tests/data/RootIndexDictionary.json
     tests/data/SubIndexDictionary.json
         from test/LibGoogleEarthTest/ -- pre-computed quadtree subindex
         fixtures, used unmodified so this port can be checked node-for-node
         against the C# implementation.

   Changes made in this port: translation from C# to Python; replacement of the
   command line interface with a library API (`availability` and `download`);
   shapely geometry input and GeoDataFrame/rasterio output; a disk response
   cache; an Esri region-query availability path. Upstream's `info` and `dump`
   commands, DXF output, terrain meshes, the non-time-machine databases and the
   `--layer-date` flag are not ported.

